<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken shares jump on share buy back.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken shares jump on share buy back.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish bank Nordbanken jumped when trading resumed at 1115 GMT Wednesday after news of a five billion crown share buy back proposal.</p>
<p>Trading was suspended ahead of the Stockholm bourse's opening on Wednesday morning but its shares jumped 9.5 crowns to 145 crowns when trading resumed.  </p>
<p>Nordbanken, a state-controlled bank, announced a share buy back scheme that could reduce the government's holding to 58 percent from 65.5 percent.</p>
<p>It said the scheme would boost earnings per share and increase its chances to expand in the restructuring of Swedish financial markets.</p>
<p>Within five minutes of trading the stock was 14.5 crowns higher at 150 crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
